  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of the <math><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></math> and the <math><msup><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> terms of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> is <math> <mrow> <mn>60</mn> </mrow> </math> and the product of its first three terms is <math> <mrow> <mn>1000.</mn> </mrow> </math> If the first term of this <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> is positive, then its <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>7</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> term is:"
  },
